1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,586
This is the Science console,

2
00:00:02,036 --> 00:00:05,435
and we've selected the hulk and pressed its Bio tab.

3
00:00:06,335 --> 00:00:08,825
That sentence in the read-out isn't the game's.

4
00:00:09,725 --> 00:00:11,386
I wrote it, in a text file,

5
00:00:11,836 --> 00:00:14,206
and it took me about a minute.

6
00:00:15,106 --> 00:00:17,792
Today you give the game two things to point at:

7
00:00:18,242 --> 00:00:20,313
some words for Science to find,

8
00:00:20,763 --> 00:00:23,571
and a place on the map that wasn't there before.

9
00:00:25,371 --> 00:00:26,745
You know these words already.

10
00:00:27,645 --> 00:00:30,851
In Lecture 7 you gave the hulk a role of your own,

11
00:00:31,301 --> 00:00:32,512
right here in this list.

12
00:00:33,412 --> 00:00:37,428
And in Lecture 8, your quest said reach derelict.

13
00:00:38,328 --> 00:00:40,466
A quest never names an object.

14
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:44,578
It names a role, and the game finds whatever wears it.

15
00:00:46,378 --> 00:00:50,594
Scan text works the same way: Scan of, derelict.

16
00:00:51,494 --> 00:00:55,514
Until now, a role always came from this file, the script.

17
00:00:56,414 --> 00:00:58,895
Today you place a thing yourself,

18
00:00:59,345 --> 00:01:02,225
and you give it its role in your own file.

19
00:01:04,025 --> 00:01:06,897
So it's one idea: give a thing a role,

20
00:01:07,347 --> 00:01:09,072
and then point at the role.

21
00:01:10,272 --> 00:01:12,037
Here's the hulk on Science today.

22
00:01:12,937 --> 00:01:17,873
Under its name it has three tab buttons, Scan, Intel and Mat,

23
00:01:18,323 --> 00:01:20,698
and each one is a record in this section.

24
00:01:21,598 --> 00:01:23,162
Two came with the template,

25
00:01:23,612 --> 00:01:26,290
and the third is yours, from Lecture 5.

26
00:01:27,190 --> 00:01:31,595
There's Hull, on the scan tab, Materials, on the mat tab,

27
00:01:32,045 --> 00:01:34,356
and Intel, on the role you added.

28
00:01:35,256 --> 00:01:36,610
There are five tabs in all:

29
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:41,057
scan, status, intel, mat, and bio.

30
00:01:41,957 --> 00:01:45,545
Each line that starts with a percent sign is one reading,

31
00:01:45,995 --> 00:01:48,888
and there are two lines here, so the game picks one.

32
00:01:50,088 --> 00:01:51,728
The hulk has three tabs,

33
00:01:52,178 --> 00:01:54,602
so I'm going to give it a fourth, called bio.

34
00:01:55,502 --> 00:01:58,202
It's the same role, a different tab,

35
00:01:58,652 --> 00:02:00,760
and this time three readings.

36
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:05,718
On Science, that's a fourth button under the hulk's name, Bio,

37
00:02:06,168 --> 00:02:08,807
and the read-out shows one of my three readings.

38
00:02:10,607 --> 00:02:12,927
There are five rules for scan text.

39
00:02:13,827 --> 00:02:15,640
One reading is one line,

40
00:02:16,090 --> 00:02:20,014
because if I press Enter in the middle, I've made two readings,

41
00:02:20,464 --> 00:02:22,297
and the crew gets half a sentence.

42
00:02:23,197 --> 00:02:25,264
One role, spelled the way the hulk wears it.

43
00:02:26,164 --> 00:02:28,479
One record for each role and tab.

44
00:02:29,379 --> 00:02:30,803
Always write a Tab line.

45
00:02:31,703 --> 00:02:33,824
And no curly brackets, at all.

46
00:02:35,624 --> 00:02:37,206
Lint checks the first four.

47
00:02:38,106 --> 00:02:40,225
The fifth it can't check,

48
00:02:40,675 --> 00:02:44,084
because curly brackets are a real feature you haven't met yet,

49
00:02:44,534 --> 00:02:47,226
so the game just shows them as you typed them.

50
00:02:48,426 --> 00:02:51,184
Everything on the map so far came from the script file,

51
00:02:51,634 --> 00:02:52,729
but this one is mine.

52
00:02:53,629 --> 00:02:55,446
Here it is on Helm's map,

53
00:02:55,896 --> 00:02:58,877
a lifeboat drifting off to one side of the hulk.

54
00:02:59,777 --> 00:03:02,227
It's a new section, with two hashes,

55
00:03:02,677 --> 00:03:05,471
and its key is this word: landmarks.

56
00:03:06,371 --> 00:03:08,385
Then comes the lifeboat's own record,

57
00:03:08,835 --> 00:03:12,522
and its name in square brackets is the name Science shows

58
00:03:12,972 --> 00:03:14,624
once the lifeboat is scanned.

59
00:03:15,524 --> 00:03:18,108
Prefab says what sort of thing it is:

60
00:03:18,558 --> 00:03:20,700
a wreck, a ship, or a station.

61
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:23,750
Roles is the label it wears.

62
00:03:24,650 --> 00:03:28,034
This is the line lint has been telling you about since Lecture 7,

63
00:03:28,484 --> 00:03:30,310
and it's the line that matters,

64
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:33,132
because it's the word everything else points at.

65
00:03:34,932 --> 00:03:36,238
Art is what it looks like.

66
00:03:36,688 --> 00:03:38,893
Lint can't check that word, so copy it.

67
00:03:39,793 --> 00:03:41,707
And Loc is where it sits:

68
00:03:42,157 --> 00:03:44,091
three numbers, in plain digits,

69
00:03:44,541 --> 00:03:46,452
with no comma inside a number.

70
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:50,284
The station is at zero, zero, zero,

71
00:03:50,734 --> 00:03:54,123
and the hulk is at zero, zero, nine thousand.

72
00:03:55,023 --> 00:03:57,721
The middle number is height, so leave it at zero.

73
00:03:58,621 --> 00:04:01,338
Mine goes here, off to one side,

74
00:04:01,788 --> 00:04:03,933
which is where you saw it on Helm's map.

75
00:04:05,733 --> 00:04:07,855
And then one line in my word list,

76
00:04:08,305 --> 00:04:09,861
so that the list stays true.

77
00:04:11,061 --> 00:04:12,980
Here's the lifeboat on Science,

78
00:04:13,430 --> 00:04:16,495
with two tab buttons under it, Scan and Intel.

79
00:04:17,395 --> 00:04:20,045
Those are the two records I'm about to write.

80
00:04:20,945 --> 00:04:22,569
The lifeboat wears a role,

81
00:04:23,019 --> 00:04:26,887
so it can have scan text: Scan of, lifeboat.

82
00:04:27,787 --> 00:04:31,413
A scan tab comes first, always, and then intel.

83
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:33,679
And that's the whole trick:

84
00:04:34,129 --> 00:04:37,139
the place and the words never mention each other.

85
00:04:38,039 --> 00:04:39,200
They both mention the role.

86
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,431
Now for the story itself.

87
00:04:43,331 --> 00:04:46,154
I add a new step, between the hulk and home,

88
00:04:46,604 --> 00:04:49,248
and it's revealed, like last time.

89
00:04:50,148 --> 00:04:51,730
I run lint before I go on,

90
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:56,569
and it says the step waits to be revealed, and nothing reveals it.

91
00:04:57,469 --> 00:04:59,298
You saw that one in Lecture 9.

92
00:05:00,198 --> 00:05:02,784
So I make one change up here:

93
00:05:03,234 --> 00:05:07,164
Close Inspection now reveals the boat, and not home.

94
00:05:08,064 --> 00:05:11,486
And it's clean, so the chain runs hulk, boat, home.

95
00:05:13,286 --> 00:05:14,544
Now look at this line:

96
00:05:14,994 --> 00:05:18,080
Done when, reach, lifeboat, five hundred.

97
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:21,927
That's a verb, a role, and a distance.

98
00:05:22,827 --> 00:05:25,176
It's the role, from the Roles line,

99
00:05:25,626 --> 00:05:28,106
and not the name the crew reads on Science.

100
00:05:29,006 --> 00:05:31,666
I gave the key the same word on purpose,

101
00:05:32,116 --> 00:05:34,116
and the next scene shows why.

102
00:05:35,916 --> 00:05:38,214
And one more line, this one for the crew.

103
00:05:39,114 --> 00:05:41,122
Here's Salvage Run in the Quest Log now,

104
00:05:41,572 --> 00:05:44,301
with a picture of DS 1 at the top of its briefing,

105
00:05:44,751 --> 00:05:46,999
because DS 1 is who gives the order.

106
00:05:47,899 --> 00:05:51,189
In the file it's one line, at the top of the briefing:

107
00:05:51,639 --> 00:05:55,238
an exclamation mark, empty square brackets,

108
00:05:55,688 --> 00:06:00,360
and then ship, colon, two slashes, and the art word for the station.

109
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:03,805
That's the same list of ships that Art comes from,

110
00:06:04,255 --> 00:06:07,983
so copy the word exactly, because lint can't check it.

111
00:06:09,183 --> 00:06:10,719
This is the one to remember.

112
00:06:11,619 --> 00:06:13,100
I take out the Roles line,

113
00:06:13,550 --> 00:06:14,963
and I get three warnings,

114
00:06:15,413 --> 00:06:17,834
one for every line that pointed at the role.

115
00:06:18,734 --> 00:06:20,486
Each one says the same thing:

116
00:06:20,936 --> 00:06:22,944
lifeboat is the landmark's key,

117
00:06:23,394 --> 00:06:25,335
and this line looks for a role.

118
00:06:26,235 --> 00:06:28,735
The key in the round brackets is not a role.

119
00:06:30,535 --> 00:06:32,314
So I put the line back.

120
00:06:33,214 --> 00:06:37,266
Next, a tab that isn't one of the five, and lint tells me.

121
00:06:38,166 --> 00:06:41,893
Then a plural: nothing wears a role called derelicts,

122
00:06:42,343 --> 00:06:44,862
and that tab would never have appeared.

123
00:06:45,762 --> 00:06:49,520
With no Loc line, the lifeboat would be sitting inside the station.

124
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:53,111
And for a section the story never asks for,

125
00:06:53,561 --> 00:06:55,146
lint reads the story too,

126
00:06:55,596 --> 00:06:58,233
and tells me which keys it does ask for.

127
00:07:00,033 --> 00:07:02,908
There are two things it can't see, and they're on the page:

128
00:07:03,358 --> 00:07:05,380
one hash on the lifeboat's heading,

129
00:07:05,830 --> 00:07:07,452
and a comma inside a number.

130
00:07:08,352 --> 00:07:10,203
Check those two by eye.

131
00:07:11,403 --> 00:07:13,854
The Quest Log has two steps showing,

132
00:07:14,304 --> 00:07:16,530
and DS 1 at the top of the briefing,

133
00:07:16,980 --> 00:07:18,551
so it's out to the hulk.

134
00:07:19,451 --> 00:07:23,858
Close Inspection is done, and there's the new step, Find the Lifeboat.

135
00:07:24,758 --> 00:07:27,300
At Science I click the hulk on the map,

136
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:30,082
and there's my fourth button, Bio,

137
00:07:30,532 --> 00:07:32,638
with one of my three readings in the read-out.

138
00:07:33,538 --> 00:07:35,160
Now it's on to the lifeboat,

139
00:07:35,610 --> 00:07:38,194
which is on the map because I wrote four lines.

140
00:07:39,094 --> 00:07:42,542
At Science again, I click the boat's icon on the map,

141
00:07:42,992 --> 00:07:45,424
and those are my words on its Scan tab.

142
00:07:46,324 --> 00:07:48,777
Its other button says Queue Intel,

143
00:07:49,227 --> 00:07:51,708
because that's a tab Science has to scan for.

144
00:07:52,608 --> 00:07:54,958
So I press it, the scan runs,

145
00:07:55,408 --> 00:07:56,738
and then that's mine too.

146
00:07:57,638 --> 00:07:59,859
In we go, and the step is done.

147
00:08:00,759 --> 00:08:02,751
Then it's home, and that's the win,

148
00:08:03,201 --> 00:08:05,392
with my Win sentence on Game results.

149
00:08:06,592 --> 00:08:09,347
Now it's your turn: place a second thing of your own,

150
00:08:09,797 --> 00:08:13,146
give it a role, and give the role some words,

151
00:08:13,596 --> 00:08:16,070
and add a step the crew can take or leave.

152
00:08:16,970 --> 00:08:19,127
Next time, we open the script file.
